  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Lesotho Country Programme Framework (2014 - 2017)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The UNIDO Country Programme (CP) described in this document constitutes the frame of reference for technical cooperation between UNIDO and the Government of Lesotho. The CP is a product of extensive and broad-based stakeholder consultations with the Government, key national stakeholders and development partners. It is an expression of a commitment by all concerned parties to work in partnership towards the attainment of the desired national objectives for industrial development. It takes into account the long-term strategy &apos;Vision 2020&apos; of Lesotho, the National Strategic Development Plan (2012# 2017) and draws upon the United Nations Development Assistance Framework (UNDAF) (2013-2017). Consistent with relevant priorities of the Government of Lesotho and in line with UNIDO&apos;s strategic focus, the programmes in the CP are organized into the following six main components: - Improving Industrial Governance: Capacity Building for Industrial Intelligence and Monitoring - Market Access through Strengthening National Quality Infrastructure in Lesotho - Value Addition of Wool and Mohair - Revitalization of Leather Value Chain - Product and Market Diversification in Textiles and Garments - Integration of Renewable Energy and Energy Efficiency in Targeted Communities  An additional component on Cleaner Production is fores</narrative>
  </description>
